  "T3": {
    "name": "T3_the_pair_phase_is_a_ratio_but_the_twist_is_physical",
    "description": "The reason is algebraic, not numerical. #207 extracts the pair phase as arg(c_mp / c_pm) -- a RATIO of two branches that traverse the SAME links. A link-uniform sign multiplies both branches equally and cancels identically, and |c_pm| is a modulus so it cancels there too (measured: phase and amplitude both unchanged to <1e-9 under an outer-bridge twist). No choice of lattice parameters can change this. Crucially this is NOT because the twist is gaugeable: it moves the spectrum by ~2.2e-02 to 2.8e-02, so the Z2 is physical here -- it simply does not enter this observable.",
